# Cite this software. GitHub renders this file as a "Cite this repository"
# button and most reference managers read it directly.
#
# TODO: add ORCIDs, and a DOI if the repository is archived on Zenodo.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: CHAPSim2 Toolkit
message: >-
  If you use this software, please cite it. The toolkit was written by
  Alex Old; please keep him as first author.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Alex
    family-names: Old
    affiliation: The University of Sheffield
    # orcid: 'https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000'
  - given-names: Wei
    family-names: Wang
    affiliation: Science and Technology Facilities Council (STFC), UKRI
    email: wei.wang@stfc.ac.uk
repository-code: 'https://github.com/weiwangstfc/CHAPSim2-toolkit'
abstract: >-
  A Python post-processing and pre-processing toolkit for the CHAPSim2
  direct numerical simulation solver. Reads CHAPSim2's XDMF, binary and
  ASCII output to produce turbulence statistics, slice and three-dimensional
  visualisation, monitor-point histories and pre-run mesh resolution
  analysis, for Cartesian and cylindrical cases with and without heat
  transfer and magnetohydrodynamics.
keywords:
  - computational fluid dynamics
  - direct numerical simulation
  - turbulence statistics
  - post-processing
  - CHAPSim2
license: BSD-3-Clause
